  "reasoning": "The widely cited figure originates from a March 2023 Goldman Sachs research report authored by Jan Hatzius and colleagues. The report estimated that generative AI could expose roughly 300 million full-time jobs worldwide to automation, based on an analysis of occupational task databases in the US and Europe. However, the study explicitly distinguished between \"exposure to automation\" and outright job replacement. Goldman Sachs noted that for most occupations, generative AI would partially automate specific tasks and act as a complement to human labor rather than replace whole jobs. Furthermore, the report highlighted that technological displacement has historically been offset by the creation of new employment and productivity gains. Stating definitively that generative AI \"will replace 300 million jobs\" distorts the findings by conflating task exposure with total job destruction.",
